# Deadly serious about having fun!

As you might know, at Rhythm Culture we are deadly serious about having fun! With this ethos in mind we are in the midst of creating a drum and dance night at the end of every ten weeks or two five week courses. It will showcase student groups, Muso Foli Dance Troupe, and local bands including Highlife (previously Hayden Hack Infusion). We have a [new video clip](/drumming-workshops/african-performances/) that we would like to share with you! The amazing Jimmy Halliday has been working closely with us over the past few months and with his super powers he has made us look amazing! You may have remembered Jimmy taking footage in class earlier this year also? Yes, that's right in the next video, we may have captured your smiling face! Keep your eye out in the next newsletter! As for other exciting news and upcoming events, the wonderful Bassidi Kone will be joining us again this year in August! Yay! We missed him last year, and we are super excited to have the opportunity to share music with him again. The experienced drummers better get ready, [African dancing](https://www.facebook.com/groups/1735722343328787/) has been grooving with Pascale Richy and have you seen David Attenborough's Great Barrier Reef, or the electric car revolution that's happening? Read on for this information and more! and most importantly get set for some deadly serious fun drumming this month folks! https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Fs\_KemsYau8
